# Build context filter for the production image (Dockerfile).
#
# Two reasons this file exists:
#
#  1. node_modules must NEVER reach the builder. The frontend stage runs `npm ci`
#     for Linux inside the image and then `COPY . .`; a host node_modules
#     directory (with platform-specific binaries from another OS) would be copied
#     straight over the correct install and break the build.
#
#  2. Restricted data must not be uploaded to a build service. The raw ADNI
#     tables are access-controlled under a Data Use Agreement, and the image does
#     not need them -- training happens locally (scripts/run_pipeline.py).
#
# The derived cohort in data/processed IS included so that a snapshot deploy
# (`railway up`, which uploads the working tree) still carries the cohort. To
# keep the dataset off the build service entirely, seed Postgres once with
# scripts/seed_db.py and uncomment the adni_cohort.json line below.

.git
.github
.gitignore
node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
.vite

# Restricted raw data: never uploaded
ADNI DATA
ADNI_DATA
adni_*
data/raw
# data/processed/adni_cohort.json

# Python / tooling scratch
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.venv
venv
env
coverage
.nyc_output
data/pipeline.log
*.log

# Secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Docs / brand renders not needed at runtime
brand_assets
architecture_pages
_preview_*.png
